+
+// The hostname a placeholder stands for, or nullopt when `address` is not one we handed out.
+NET_EXPORT std::optional<std::string> Socks5UdpRelayHostForPlaceholder(
+    const IPAddress& address);
+
+// A connected datagram socket that relays through a SOCKS5 proxy. Used by QuicSessionPool for
+// sessions whose chain is a SOCKS5 proxy (see above).
+//
+// Connect() binds a local UDP socket and starts the association; writes made before it is up are
+// queued (the synchronous QUIC path). ConnectAsync() completes only once the association is up or
+// has failed, so a proxy that refuses UDP ASSOCIATE fails the QUIC job and the request carries on
+// over TCP, exactly as a network that blocks UDP would.
+//
+// The peer may be a placeholder (sent as a hostname) or a real IP literal (an IP-literal origin).
